    "title": "The E Form: The Box You Already Own",
    "summary": "The E form's twelve pentatonic dots are the shape most guitarists already play at fret 5, and only four of the twelve sit outside the Am chord — the fewest of any window in the chapter.",
    "tags": ["caged", "minor"],
    "readingTimeMin": 4,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The E form of A minor is "
        },
        {
          "text": "the barre at fret 5",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-triad-e-form"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " you already know: "
        },
        {
          "text": "5 7 7 5 5 5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Its pentatonic window is the same one chapter 2 used for the triad — frets "
        },
        {
          "text": "4–8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — and its twelve dots sit on only three of those five frets: "
        },
        {
          "text": "5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Nothing at fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", nothing at fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
